  "seoBody": "<h2>Is TrueContext the same as ProntoForms?</h2><p>Yes. TrueContext is the platform formerly known as ProntoForms. The product and the commercial model did not change with the name.</p><h2>How much does TrueContext cost?</h2><p>The published entry tier, Digital, starts at 400 US dollars a month for the whole team, billed annually. The Intelligent and Elite tiers above it are custom priced. Their own pricing page states that it is not a per-user-per-month tool and that pricing is based on organisation size, operational complexity and tier, so you need a quote.</p><h2>Why look for a TrueContext alternative?</h2><p>Commitment and comparability. You buy a year before you know whether your team will use the app, and you cannot compare the cost against anything without a sales conversation. For a smaller UK firm that is a lot of risk to carry up front.</p><h2>What does Quickler charge instead?</h2><p>£50 per active user a month with a £50 monthly minimum, billed monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit. No annual commitment, no setup fee. An active user is someone who completed at least two Checks that month, so occasional users cost nothing. The free tier is 20 reports a month, free forever, with no card.</p><h2>What is TrueContext better at?</h2><p>Enterprise integration, clearly. Salesforce, ServiceNow and similar platforms connect properly, so a completed job updates the system of record without anyone retyping it. If that is your requirement, TrueContext is built for it and Quickler is not an integration platform.</p>",
